  "issue_number": 128,
  "issue_title": "feat: sync remote train/eval artifacts back to local workspace",
  "issue_body": "## Problem\n\nTrain and eval jobs run on the remote GPU host, but the results stay on the remote machine after the run finishes.\nThat makes it hard to inspect, archive, or commit the artifacts from the local workspace.\n\n## Goal\n\nAfter each finished train/eval run, automatically copy the final artifacts back into the local repo workspace.\n\n## Expected behavior\n\n- remote train outputs are copied back to the local `experiments/...` or `test_logs/...` folder\n- remote eval outputs are copied back to the local `test_logs/...` folder\n- include the result files such as:\n  - `best_theta.npy`\n  - `summary.json`\n  - `history.json`\n  - `eval.json`\n  - `cost_ledger.jsonl`\n- preserve the remote run directory structure\n- fail clearly if the remote copy step fails\n\n## Why this matters\n\nRight now the final results are produced on the remote GPU box, but the local machine does not get the artifacts automatically.\nThat slows down review, archiving, and PR submission.\n\n## Suggested implementation\n\n- add a post-run sync step to `scripts/run_remote.sh` or a wrapper script\n- allow the destination path to be configured with an env var\n- keep the sync optional for users who only want remote execution\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- a completed remote train run leaves the final artifacts locally\n- a completed remote eval run leaves the final artifacts locally\n- the sync step is logged clearly\n- existing remote execution still works if sync is disabled\n",
  "merged_at": "2026-07-12T23:44:59.000Z",
